; form-lower-string-band — STRING SCAN LOWERING in the Form -> assembly compiler:
; the fstr-find-loop rung, receipts/2026-09-02-directive-ledger-walked.md's named
; frontier ("the fstr per-byte family (398k hot): fkwu has NO native
; substring/char_at/str_find — the per-byte recipes are the only door, and 0 of
; the current hot worklist is coverable... the walked-direction fix is form-lower
; coverage growth (strings)"). This band is that growth, proven on REAL EXECUTED
; arm64 bytes (not byte-image equality alone, the way form-lower-streq-band.fk
; proves STR_EQ): lo-strfind-embed-str compiles two Form strings + core.fk's
; fstr-find-loop/fstr-find-eq-at shape into one native leaf, mmap'd and CALLED
; through the body's own JIT door (jit_leaf_inram), and its answer is checked
; against core.fk's own str_find on the SAME strings.
;
; GROUNDING, so the design does not need re-deriving (form-lower.fk's own header
; over lo-str-bytes/lo-strfind-core carries the same note): jit_leaf_inram — the
; only door from Form into crystallized bytes — declines any non-integer
; argument (probed live: a string argument, or a string inside the arg list,
; both answer `nothing`), and there is no relocation table for compiled bytes to
; call back into a C native by address. lo-streq already answered this design
; question for the string family by INLINING str_eq's loop over raw pointers,
; never calling the native; this recipe makes that same choice EXECUTABLE by
; embedding both strings' bytes in the image itself (fa-movz+fa-strb into a
; stack buffer the prologue opens) — the same self-contained-constant idiom
; fa-mov-imm64 already uses for float literals, extended byte-wise. No new
; native, no new call-out tag, no runtime/fkwu-uni.c change. The one real
; addition is a new arm64 instruction encoding, fa-sxtw (form-asm.fk) — closing
; the SAME 32-bit ABI-return wall jit-leaf-inram-band.fk's own header already
; names (a negative w0 zero-extends across fk_inram_call's 64-bit return);
; without it every not-found case here would read 4294967295, not -1.
;
; SCOPE, NAMED: both strings are compile-time constants of the recipe (embedded
; at lowering time); `from` is not threaded through — every scan starts at 0.
; Runtime (non-embedded) string arguments are the named next stone, gated on a
; native call-out door this pass did not need and should not invent unread.
;
; PROOF LEVEL: FOURTH-ARM ONLY — jit_leaf_inram is a runtime-fkwu door (the same
; footing as jit-leaf-inram-band.fk). Under the three sibling kernels the name
; folds to `nothing` and every claim below would read green while proving
; nothing.
;
; Verdict 63 when the string family lowers and executes correctly:
;   1   a real scan: "fox" found in a full sentence, native == interpreted
;   2   an empty haystack: bound<=0 decided at lowering time, native == -1 ==
;       interpreted (the trivial 4-instruction path, not the loop)
;   4   a not-found search: the needle is absent, native == -1 == interpreted
;   8   a full-length match: needle == haystack, native == 0 == interpreted
;   16  the trivial (bound<=0) image is byte-identical to the clang/otool
;       oracle for movz/sub/sxtw/ret — CONVICTION FULL on the new instruction
;   32  COMPOSITIONAL — the full-loop image's byte length equals the exact
;       formula (prologue + 2*(hlen+nlen) embed bytes + 2 pointer setup + the
;       27-instruction core), and ends in ret — no instruction is unaccounted
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/form-asm.fk form-stdlib/form-lower.fk

(do
    (defn flsb-check (h n)
        (do (let img (lo-strfind-embed-str h n))
            (let native (jit_leaf_inram img 0))
            (let interp (str_find h n 0))
            (eq native interp)))

    ; c0: a real scan over a real (prose) string
    (let c0 (if (flsb-check "the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog" "fox") 1 0))

    ; c1: an empty haystack (the bound<=0 lowering-time path)
    (let c1 (if (flsb-check "" "needle") 2 0))

    ; c2: a not-found search (needle absent, haystack non-empty)
    (let c2 (if (flsb-check "hello world" "xyz") 4 0))

    ; c3: a full-length match (needle == haystack)
    (let c3 (if (flsb-check "matched" "matched") 8 0))

    ; c4: byte-conviction on the trivial (bound<=0) image — the assembler's own
    ; reference (clang/otool oracle: movz w0,#0 ; sub w0,w0,#1 ; sxtw x0,w0 ; ret)
    (let trivial-img (lo-strfind-embed "" (lo-str-bytes "x")))
    (let trivial-ref (list 0 0 128 82   0 4 0 81   0 124 64 147   192 3 95 214))
    (let c4 (if (eq (fa-conviction trivial-img trivial-ref) 1) 16 0))

    ; c5: compositional — the full-loop image length equals the exact formula,
    ; and it ends in ret. "abc"/"bc": 1 (sub sp) + 2*3 (embed h) + 2*2 (embed n)
    ; + 2 (pointer setup) + 27 (the fixed core) = 40 instructions = 160 bytes.
    (let loop-img (lo-strfind-embed-str "abc" "bc"))
    (let expected-len (mul 4 (add (add 1 (mul 2 (add 3 2))) (add 2 27))))
    (let n (len loop-img))
    (let c5 (if (eq n expected-len)
            (if (eq (nth loop-img (sub n 4)) 192)
            (if (eq (nth loop-img (sub n 1)) 214) 32 0) 0) 0))

    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 (add c3 (add c4 c5))))))
